<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila stocks slide 1.23 pct on U.S. rate fears.</title>
<headline>Manila stocks slide 1.23 pct on U.S. rate fears.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>------------------------- April 22 ----------------------------</p>
<p>			 * All sectors drop</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Manila stocks slumped at midsession on Tuesday due to jitters of a U.S. rate hike and fears of a local property bust, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Rumours that a property firm is near bankruptcy and prospects of a rise in the U.S. rate continue to depress the market,&quot; said a trader in a local brokerage house.</p>
<p>The main index fell 36.17 points to 2,908.81 after one hour of trade.</p>
